id: pm-rl-evalplans
title: Enforce predeclared causal evaluation plans at promotion
description: "Declare target populations, correlation units, sample sizes and fixed stopping rules before experiments. Bind plan identity and clustered observations to comparison and generation promotion."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:36:09.182Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T21:53:39.246Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Synthetic correlated cohorts cannot masquerade as independent samples; changed plans invalidate comparison identity. Typed SDK and CLI; compact TOON/JSON; typed refusals with remedies; README and example; non-git real public-tracker validation; npm and Bun CI release gates.
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:36:11.512Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against the pinned CLI SDK declarations and sibling package sources/docs: core Plan/Decision stores decisions but has no causal experiment-plan enforcement; pm-jev owns model calibration/evaluation; pm-context supplies context. Existing pm-rl-rsipower supplies one powered dataset and is retained separately. This item adds reusable immutable plan/comparison enforcement and cluster-aware promotion, stacked on PR #94; must merge after #94. Dependency pins remain unchanged. Local verification will be targeted tests, typecheck and lint; full npm/Bun release gates run in CI due shared CPU load."
  "2026-10-21T21:49:50.172Z",codex-agent,"Implemented fixed paired plans in core Plan records, immutable result Decisions, provenance-pinned comparison identities, and authoritative promotion enforcement. Plans pin incumbent provenance, populations, member-to-unit assignments, sample sizes, fixed stopping, objective and criterion. Equal-unit aggregation counts correlated cohorts once; one sealed result per plan. Existing unplanned controllers retain legacy semantics without causal-plan claims. Non-git public validation measured 95 observations as one repository unit: candidate 0.7684210526 vs incumbent 0.2315789474; naive episode-count gate would promote, clustered gate refuses. Read-only public source digest is unchanged; evidence is descriptive replay, not deployed causal benefit."
  "2026-10-21T21:51:52.718Z",codex-agent,"Verification: node --test test/evaluation-plan.test.ts test/promotion.test.ts passes 30/30 with zero skipped. New module focused coverage passes 100 percent lines/branches/functions; full four-dimension gate remains for CI. npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run duplicates (zero clones), npm run docstring (49 files; 342 declarations) pass. pm test --run --progress ran the linked correlated-cohort regression successfully (1/1). Behavioral revert proof: changing only evaluatePlan to count episode rows fails the correlated-cohort regression; removing only the authoritative enforcement call fails the real promotion regression. Both reverted variants exit 1; exact source bytes restored and 30/30 rerun passes. Local strict health exposes existing extension skew and fence drift in this shared clone, plus advisory stale/provenance findings; no history or merge repair performed. Fresh CI health and npm/Bun release matrices are required before handoff."
  "2026-10-21T21:53:39.245Z",codex-agent,"Packed real-CLI acceptance also passes on the same read-only public snapshot in a non-git scratch tracker, with no Git executable for plan register/show/evaluate. Measured JSON evaluation output is 780 bytes and TOON plan summary is 280 bytes for the 95-item cohort. Source digest remains unchanged. Report and reproducible acceptance runner are linked. No new CLI/SDK defect was found; existing shared-clone health limitations are separate from fresh CI evidence."
